# Project intelligence

Record verified project facts here before installation: project purpose, stack,
source locations, exact local verification commands, integration/production
branches, and the authoritative release runbook. Preserve project-owned facts,
vendor/generated sections, safety constraints and local extensions during updates.

The distribution engine adds marked shared RPI policy and conditional rule blocks.
Those blocks have one canonical source under `templates/rules/` and
`templates/instructions/`; never create a reverse dependency on CLAUDE.md.
Claude reads the shared facts through its CLAUDE.md import. Codex reads AGENTS.md
natively, with root-to-current-directory discovery and its configured byte limit.

Version curated research, approved plans, phase files, decisions and handoffs.
Raw machine inventories, telemetry and transient recovery data stay local.
Operational report tracking follows repository visibility (Rule #70).
